.TH AURAPASS-BRIDGE 1 "2026" "aurapass 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aurapass-bridge \- serve an AuraPass vault to browser extensions over localhost
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aurapass-bridge
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aurapass-bridge
keeps an encrypted vault unlocked and answers the AuraPass browser extensions
over a WebSocket bound to
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
The desktop application embeds the same server; this binary exists for
machines with no graphical session.
.PP
Every frame is sealed with XChaCha20-Poly1305 under a key derived from the
pairing token, and the listener never binds a routable address. The token is
stored in the configuration file with mode 0600.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vault " " \fIFILE\fR
Vault file to open. Defaults to the most recently used vault.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port to listen on. Falls back to the next free port if busy.
.TP
.BR \-\-password-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the master password from a file instead of prompting.
.TP
.BR \-\-password-stdin
Read the master password from standard input.
.TP
.BR \-\-password-env
Allow reading the master password from
.BR $AURAPASS_MASTER_PASSWORD .
.TP
.BR \-\-key-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Key file required to unlock the vault.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-remote-unlock
Start locked and let the extension unlock the vault. Off by default, because
anyone holding the pairing token could then guess the master password.
.TP
.B \-\-lock-on-disconnect
Lock the vault when the last extension disconnects.
.TP
.B \-\-print-token
Print the pairing token and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-rotate-token
Replace the pairing token, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Use an alternative configuration directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aurapass (1),
.BR aurapass-desktop (1),
.BR aurapass-native-host (1)
